  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 132 AM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nAs of 1:30 AM CST, temperatures across the area are in the upper\n30s with winds out of the north between 10 and 15 mph. Some \npatchy fog will be possible this morning along and on the \nPrairie Coteau of northeast SD and in north central SD along the\nMissouri River, although confidence is low as winds look to \nstay a little too strong. Visibilities reductions down to about \na mile are expected if fog does develop.\n\nNot a whole lot is going on during the forecast. Temperatures today \nand Friday will be the coolest of the period with highs in the 40s, \npossibly reaching the low 50s west river. WAA then takes over Friday \nevening through the weekend to bring highs up to about 10-15 degrees \nabove normal. This looks to stay in place into at least the first \nhalf of next work week. Fog is more likely tonight into Friday \nmorning across central SD as winds are much weaker and skies are \nclearer. Visibilities around a half mile or less will be possible.",
